From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Keep the PCR on the video stream

mpegtsmux puts the PCR on the first stream it creates, and it creates
streams only for pads that already have caps. When the first AAC frame
reaches it before the encoder's caps, the PCR is carried by the audio stream
for the whole session. Audio comes in 40 ms bursts, so PCRs then arrive in
bursts with gaps of over 100 ms, and in a replica of the pipeline 28 to 33%
of the packets left late. It happened in 4 of about 36 runs.

The muxer now gets a program map that places both streams in program 1, as
before, and names the video pad as the PCR stream. The PAT and PMT are
unchanged: program 1 at PMT PID 0x20 with the PCR on PID 0x1011.

diff -ruN a/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c b/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
--- a/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
+++ b/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
@@ -523,6 +523,21 @@
                 "alignment", (gint) 7, /* Force the correct alignment for UDP */
                 NULL);
 
+  /* Both streams in program 1, as before, with the PCR on video. Without a
+   * map the muxer puts the PCR on whichever stream it creates first, and when
+   * sound reaches it before the encoder's caps it stays on the audio stream
+   * for the whole session: PCRs then come in bursts with gaps of over 100 ms,
+   * and the receiver's clock stumbles. */
+  {
+    g_autoptr(GstStructure) prog_map = gst_structure_new ("prog-map",
+                                                          "sink_4113", G_TYPE_INT, 1,
+                                                          "sink_4352", G_TYPE_INT, 1,
+                                                          "PCR_1", G_TYPE_STRING, "sink_4113",
+                                                          NULL);
+
+    g_object_set (mpegmux, "prog-map", prog_map, NULL);
+  }
+
 
   queue_pre_payloader = gst_element_factory_make ("queue", "wfd-pre-payloader-queue");
   success &= gst_bin_add (bin, queue_pre_payloader);
